        1670,
        1849
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "(g) Act for, on behalf of and at the direction of\nthe Mayor in the exercise of all functions, powers and duties\nwhich the Mayor may have pursuant to the New York City Loan\nGuarantee Act of 1978, P. L. 95-339, as the same may be from\ntime to time amended, an Agreement to Guarantee by and among\nthe United States of America, the State of New York, The City\nof New York, the New York State Financial Control Board and the\nMunicipal Assistance Corporation for The City of New York, a\nGuaranteed Bond Purchase Agreement by and among The City of\nNew York, certain City pension funds, certain State pension\nfunds and the United States of America, each dated as of\nNovember 15, 1978, a Loan Agreement dated as of July 20, 1979,\nbetween The City of New York and certain banks, and any other\nseasonal financing agreement of The City of New York, including,\nbut not limited to, full power to execute for, on behalf of, and\nat the direction of the Mayor, any document pursuant to any such\nagreement and any agreement, amendment to such agreement or other\ndocument pursuant to such law. The exercise of functions, powers\nand duties for, on behalf of, and at the direction of the Mayor\nby such Deputy Mayor pursuant to this delegation shall not require\nthe consent in writing of the Mayor or any other official of the\nCity.",
